Could we short-circuit a trailing `*` in `globMatches()` instead of special-casing only `"*"` here? Once the matcher reaches a final `*`, the remaining input must match. This also avoids scanning the remaining value for patterns like `"foo*"` and `"foo?*"`.

The existing star branch could become:

```java
if (patternCodePoint == '*') {
  patternIndex += Character.charCount(patternCodePoint);
  if (patternIndex == pattern.length()) {
    return true;
  }
  patternIndexAfterStar = patternIndex;
  valueIndexAfterStar = valueIndex;
  continue;
}
```

Then this special case in `createGlobPredicate()` can be removed.

